WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.568
-White House press secretary
Sarah Huckabee Sanders

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:03.870
has been holding
a lot of press briefings lately,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.738
but I don't think
all the questions

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:07.506
we need answered
have been asked.

00:00:07.506 --> 00:00:10.577
So we decided to hold another
one right here, right now.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.011
That's right,
Sarah Huckabee Sanders

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:14.013
and the "Late Night" press corps
are here in our studio

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:15.114
and ready to go.

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:16.549
So without further ado,

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:19.118
it's time for the "Late Night
White House Press Briefing."

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:21.120
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:27.560
♪♪

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.162
Yes, Ms. Sanders, Ms. Sanders!

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.663
Ms. Sanders!
Yes, yes, thank you.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:33.065
Seth Meyers,
"Late Night with Seth Meyers."

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:35.601
Secretary Sanders,
what are the most terrifying

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:38.171
nine words
in the English language?

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:40.139
-The President will still
be here in five years.

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:47.279
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:47.279 --> 00:00:48.614
-Next question.

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:51.851
What does Trump ask for
when he goes into Supercuts?

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.686
-Upside-down and inside-out.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:56.022
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:59.224
-Secretary Sanders, did you have
a nice Thanksgiving?

00:00:59.224 --> 00:01:01.828
-I want to share a few things
that I'm thankful for.

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:05.398
And I think it would be nice
for you guys to do so, as well.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:08.267
-Okay. I'm thankful
we can use clever editing

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:11.604
to make this nightmare of an
administration sound silly.

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.139
-You're not fixing the problem.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.607
You're only making things worse.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.642
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:18.778
-That's fair.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:19.945
What did Eric Trump say

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:22.081
when he showed up
for Thanksgiving dinner?

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:23.149
-"Happy Halloween."

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:26.919
[ Laughter ]
-Ah.

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:29.656
Yeah.
So close.

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:32.058
So close.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:34.327
When was the last time
someone tried to drump --

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.195
tried to jump
the White House fence,

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:37.496
and who was it?

00:01:37.496 --> 00:01:39.998
-This afternoon,
the First Lady and Barron Trump.

00:01:39.998 --> 00:01:43.203
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:45.605
-If Melania could trade places
with any person,

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:46.806
who would it be?

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:49.008
-All of us in this room
and across this country.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:52.645
-But given her choice, what
would be Melania's dream job?

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:53.646
-A single mother.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:58.518
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:02.721
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:02.721 --> 00:02:04.323
-If I can switch the focus

00:02:04.323 --> 00:02:06.325
to the Democratic party
for a second,

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:08.261
how did a young Bernie Sanders

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:10.530
first arrive
in Washington, D.C.?

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.898
-Via horse-drawn wagon.

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:15.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:19.072
-How often does the President
lie on Twitter?

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.906
-For the third or fourth time,
just today,

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:22.408
as well as 10 or 15 times

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.943
on both Thursday and Friday
of last week.

00:02:24.943 --> 00:02:32.351
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:32.351 --> 00:02:34.520
-How would you describe Ivanka?

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.922
-Very basic.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.922 --> 00:02:38.958
[ Audience groans ]

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.260
-Oooh.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.230
What does Paul Ryan think about
while he's having sex?

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.532
-President Reagan's
1981 tax cuts.

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:50.803
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:53.806
-Who's worse --
Bill Cosby or Bill O'Reilly?

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:56.075
-Both Bills achieved
the President's priorities.

00:02:56.075 --> 00:03:00.212
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:02.615
-Who do you call
when Steve Bannon gets loose

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.350
and is running around
the White House?

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.818
-The Fish and Wildlife Service.

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:08.120
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.791
-How does the President's
urologist describe Donald Trump?

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:12.892
-A small business owner.

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:14.994
-Well, it looks like
we're out of time,

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:17.397
so on behalf of the rest of the
press corps, have a great night.

